{"agent":"impl-salvage-bf797","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_gate_outcome` computes the gate outcome from only `best.findings`, while the caller still chooses `best = min(results, key=lambda r: r.status)`. On a converged full re-review with two `RV.REVIEWED` results, if the first result contains only below-floor findings (e.g. one `LOW`) and the second result contains a `HIGH` finding, `RV.blocking_findings(best.findings, converged=True, floor=\"HIGH\")` returns empty and `_gate_outcome` returns `\"passed\"`, silently ignoring the other reviewer’s `HIGH` finding. Before this change, the first result’s `LOW` finding made `best.findings` truthy and the gate failed; the new convergence rule turns that previously failing state into a false pass whenever the first status-minimal result is non-blocking. The convergence decision must aggregate blocking findings across all reviewed results, not only the first status-minimal one.","digest":"c4f1f5aa7137bde7","location":"ddflow/api/review.py:_gate_outcome","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review.py:_gate_outcome"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test claims to prove that the HIGH convergence floor is not a free pass, but its second review call is `_review(repo)` without `full=True`. The file’s own convergence comment says a delta or fix round blocks at any severity, so this assertion can pass even when the convergence/full path is broken: for example, if `blocking_findings` used `>` instead of `>=` against the floor, a full converged round would incorrectly pass a new HIGH finding, while this non-full delta/fix review would still block for the unrelated reason that delta/fix rounds block everything. Thus the test does not actually guard the claimed “new HIGH in a converged later round still blocks” behavior.","digest":"6f03ca5efe2f91dc","location":"tests/test_review_convergence.py:test_a_later_rounds_new_high_finding_still_blocks","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_review_convergence.py:test_a_later_rounds_new_high_finding_still_blocks"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16445,"diff_sha":"385f68340174f93296a99a139592b9522f2174889aa8ea31182f26bfa0bdc933","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":390.5,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"7ffca10b8b8d3e6a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bf797745b5a.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261031T100806Z-0df3b969.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"3a4da3b45aaaf93ee8431396870da8a1a3e8b2fb","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review.py":"100644 91f9ee1aabb2ff22b65da1a50985f834872cc29c","ddflow/config_sections/review.py":"100644 af705e87db5d8e7d0e4d21a51294a5f0b3c3696e","ddflow/services/review.py":"100644 de6851822e43345bfa8bb69565b81943ce02e50b","tests/test_review_convergence.py":"100644 38e7e6e8c23c875efac7ff8c5dc94a59ac292092"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review.py:_gate_outcome","tests/test_review_convergence.py:test_a_later_rounds_new_high_finding_still_blocks"],"tree_sha":"16e80505b24f+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e7c80f1f298d62764526b2791","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":118238,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bf797745b5a","ts":"2026-10-31T10:33:58.340339Z"}
