{"agent":"impl-salvage-bf797","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new pooling of findings only happens when `converged_round` is true; the conservative `else best.findings` branch preserves the same ignored-finding bug on the non-converged path. With two `RV.REVIEWED` results where `best` (the first result when statuses tie under `min(results, key=lambda r: r.status)`) has no findings and the second `RV.REVIEWED` result has a `HIGH` finding, `found` is `best.findings` (empty), so the `if not found` branch returns `\"passed\"` before the second reviewer’s `HIGH` is ever examined. A normal non-converged review can therefore pass despite a HIGH finding.","digest":"673daf79761ba9a1","location":"ddflow/api/review.py:_gate_outcome","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review.py:_gate_outcome"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test claims to verify that the floor paragraph is only sent where the floor applies, but it only calls `api._floor_lines(\"\")` and `api._floor_lines(\"HIGH\")`; it never calls `_floor_for` or the prompt-building code path. If `_floor_for` incorrectly returns `\"HIGH\"` for a delta/fix round, the bug this test is named for would still occur (the paragraph would still be sent), yet both assertions pass because `_floor_lines(\"HIGH\")` still contains `\"below HIGH severity\"`. The test therefore does not fail on the unfixed prompt-gating behavior and does not protect the path it was added to cover.","digest":"7661038a6b0077dc","location":"tests/test_review_convergence.py:test_the_floor_paragraph_is_only_sent_where_the_floor_applies","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_review_convergence.py:test_the_floor_paragraph_is_only_sent_where_the_floor_applies"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":18185,"diff_sha":"d5a82a29173a155f9255123443b90f8ec8d551cae2f36dfc7764f550f6256ee0","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED